 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+
+## Section navigation
+
+Top News, World, Politics, Multimedia, and Reports share a server-rendered shell. All five panels are rendered on entry; client-side navigation changes their `hidden` state without replacing or detaching DOM nodes. React islands and local UI state survive section switches. Hidden panels leave the layout and accessibility tree, and islands using `client:visible` hydrate when shown. This trades a larger initial document for section switches without network requests or remounts.
+
+Each section has a direct URL under the configured Astro base path. The controller updates the page title and active navigation link, moves focus into the selected panel, and restores per-section scroll positions, including on Back/Forward. Normal links remain usable without JavaScript. Navigation to article, category, and account pages leaves the section shell and follows the existing page routing.
